<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive icon foreground layer - wraps the exact, unmodified production logo
  (memory_architect_logo.png) rather than a redrawn/simplified motif, per the explicit "use exactly
  this image, do not redesign" requirement.

  The 22dp inset on every side is not a crop - it is the only way to guarantee zero clipping under
  Android's adaptive icon system: every launcher (circle/squircle/rounded-square/OEM-specific) masks
  the outer ring of the 108dp x 108dp canvas, and even mask-safe content can still be nudged by
  launcher parallax. Google's own guidance is to keep all meaningful artwork inside a 66dp safe zone
  centered in the 108dp canvas (66/108 = a ~21dp margin per side) - 22dp here gives a small extra
  safety buffer over that minimum. The source artwork's own badge shape fills its 1254x1254 canvas
  almost edge-to-edge (~1.5% built-in margin) - nowhere near enough on its own - so without this
  inset, every circular-mask launcher would cut into the brain icon, the puzzle-piece mark, and the
  "MEMORIZE - REBUILD - MASTER" wordmark at the bottom.

  This inset is the ADAPTIVE launcher icon's own accommodation for a platform constraint - it is not
  applied to the legacy mipmap-*dpi/ic_launcher.png icons (full-bleed, exact source image, no inset)
  or to the splash screen/in-app usages (see SplashScreen.kt), which reference
  memory_architect_logo.png directly since neither is system-masked. See the area outside this inset
  is simply not drawn (transparent), letting ic_launcher_background.xml's matching dark gradient
  show through with no visible seam - see that file's own doc.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/memory_architect_logo"
    android:insetLeft="22dp"
    android:insetTop="22dp"
    android:insetRight="22dp"
    android:insetBottom="22dp" />

